  "name": "HLA - PANEL REACTIVE IgG ANTIBODIES (PRA) CLASS II QUANTITATIVE",
  "code": "2374",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1012\" data-end=\"1127\">\n<p data-start=\"1014\" data-end=\"1127\"><strong data-start=\"1014\" data-end=\"1033\">Low PRA (&lt; 20%)</strong>: Indicates minimal sensitization to HLA Class II antigens. Suitable for most donor matches.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1128\" data-end=\"1241\">\n<p data-start=\"1130\" data-end=\"1241\"><strong data-start=\"1130\" data-end=\"1155\">Moderate PRA (20&ndash;80%)</strong>: Indicates moderate immune sensitization. Matching may be limited; caution advised.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1242\" data-end=\"1386\">\n<p data-start=\"1244\" data-end=\"1386\"><strong data-start=\"1244\" data-end=\"1264\">High PRA (&gt; 80%)</strong>: Indicates strong sensitization to HLA antigens; high risk of antibody-mediated rejection. Limited donor compatibility.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
